---
/* What niwa is, in the words the site already publishes.
 *
 * One claim, one paragraph, and the three nouns under it. The section makes
 * no promise the documentation does not keep, so it borrows nothing from
 * anywhere else.
 *
 * The three nouns are not a feature list. They are the answer to the only
 * question a reader has at this point — what does "what the machine should
 * be" actually cover — and they are the four words the paragraph above
 * would otherwise have to spend a sentence on.
 */
---

<section class="why" id="why" aria-labelledby="why-title">
  <div>
    <h2 id="why-title">A setup you can read.</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="why-body">
    <p>
      niwa is a configuration tool for macOS. One Luau script declares what the machine
      should be. Applying it makes that true.
    </p>
    <ul class="why-covers">
      <li>Packages</li>
      <li>Dotfiles</li>
      <li>Settings</li>
      <li>Services</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
